{
  "id": "COMPOUND:25961 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Isopreleosibirone is implicated in the biological activity against A549 cells through a multi-step mechanism. The evidence suggests that Isopreleosibirone targets the Nuclear factor NF-kappa-B complex, which is a key regulator of inflammatory and pro-survival signaling in cancer cells. This complex is subsequently targeted by Ethyl ethyl-d5 sulfide, a compound that in turn affects A549 cells. Additionally, Isopreleosibirone is also shown to target A2780cisR, a cell line variant of A549, which is further targeted by galloyl(-6)Glc(b)-O-Ph(3,5-diOMe,4-OH), another compound that influences A549. These findings collectively indicate that Isopreleosibirone exerts its effects on A549 through a series of molecular interactions that involve both direct and indirect pathways, ultimately contributing to its potential therapeutic impact on this cell line.",
